1
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,000
Aiyet

2
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:20,680
What?

3
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:22,400
What’s wrong with you again?

4
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:28,160
Aiyet

5
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,480
Come out here right now!

6
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:42,560
Aiyet

7
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:46,160
Hao Ruichi

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:53,400
You...

9
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:56,320
Your nosebleed... it's blue?

10
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,800
You're really an alien!

11
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,960
His crystal is still intact!

12
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:26,160
You’re definitely not from here.

13
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,280
If you still don’t believe it,

14
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:32,640
then there’s something seriously wrong with your IQ.

15
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:34,640
Oh my god!

16
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:36,960
You messing up my life all the time is one thing,

17
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,280
but don’t make it this bizarre!

18
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:41,960
Wait a second...

19
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:44,840
If...

20
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:47,440
you’re not from around here,

21
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,680
then why did you come to Earth?

22
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,920
You're not planning to experiment on me, right?

23
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,000
I...

24
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,240
am here to capture a fugitive.

25
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,480
Capture someone?

26
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,720
A highly dangerous fugitive from Lanke Star

27
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:09,040
escaped to Earth.

28
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,520
I followed him here.

29
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:22,600
Aiyet

30
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,240
Never would I have thought,

31
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,680
that I, Aiyet,

32
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:33,320
could draw the attention of a true Lanke Star Envoy to come after me.

33
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,040
You can't defeat me.

34
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:37,040
Come back with me quietly.

35
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:38,560
I know I can’t beat you.

36
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,160
But Lanke Star...

37
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:41,800
I don’t want to spend another second there.

38
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,560
Goodbye!

39
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,160
Your Excellency the Envoy,

40
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,440
Aiyet!

41
00:02:58,840 --> 00:02:59,880
I order you to stop!

42
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,680
Goodbye, Hao Ruichi.

43
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:03,520
I’ll never go back again.

44
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:04,880
Preparing for teleportation...

45
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,520
Intergalactic jump to unknown coordinates...

46
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,320
Highly dangerous.

47
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:08,400
Please proceed with caution.

48
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,600
Teleportation.

49
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,560
That's so amazing!

50
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:30,840
A face is also made of flesh.

51
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:33,280
Then how are we any different?

52
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:35,360
Could it be...

53
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,080
That the body's structure is different?

54
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:40,160
Qi Miao,

55
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,760
don't test my limits.

56
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,440
Sorry!

57
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,280
I just got too excited for a moment.

58
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:49,680
Anyway,

59
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,520
until I capture the fugitive

60
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,800
and fully replenish my energy,

61
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,600
I'll have to stay here.

62
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,080
So,

63
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,440
I hope you adjust your attitude

64
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,680
and stop treating me

65
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,800
like some kind of pervert.

66
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:09,040
Living together all the time—

67
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,720
isn't that really dangerous?

68
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:17,640
Living with me is your good fortune.

69
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:18,720
Besides,

70
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,800
I need your help to replenish my crystal energy.

71
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:21,760
Replenish energy?

72
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:23,800
Exactly.

73
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:26,240
We Lankexing people, when on other planets,

74
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,080
rely on energy crystals

75
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,200
to release energy.

76
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,200
And you,

77
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,280
like me, are an Omega-type person.

78
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,040
So your magnetic field can help restore my energy.

79
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:38,520
Omega-type person?

80
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:39,760
Of course.

81
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,000
You Earthlings can't see your own magnetic fields—

82
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:42,960
that's completely normal.

83
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:44,720
But from what I've observed,

84
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,160
your magnetic fields are divided into hundreds of types.

85
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:50,480
And yours happens to be the same type as mine.

86
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,240
I'm just usually unlucky.

87
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,960
So, does that mean you're as unlucky as I am?

88
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:55,040
No.

89
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:56,880
What you call 'luck'

90
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:58,480
has nothing to do with the type of magnetic field.

91
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,440
The reason you're unlucky

92
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,680
is because of your mindset,

93
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,080
your actions,

94
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:05,320
which cause the gaps in your magnetic field to widen.

95
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:08,040
I can help you

96
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,160
fill in the magnetic field gaps.

97
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,800
The gap is widening.

98
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,560
I can't understand a thing!

99
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:17,680
Can I interpret it as

100
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,480
you can help me change my luck?

101
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:21,240
That's right.

102
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,160
As long as you follow my instructions obediently,

103
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:29,160
I can help you change your luck.

104
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,440
Change my luck?

105
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:39,320
And you're making me spend money?

106
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,760
I just spent half my monthly salary!

107
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,320
Shopping can change my luck?

108
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:46,040
No,

109
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:47,440
I simply need new clothes.

110
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,280
Wait,

111
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,160
didn't you promise to help me change my luck?

112
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:51,880
Yes.

113
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,440
Haven't you noticed?

114
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,760
Since this morning,

115
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:57,680
your luck has already shifted.

116
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,200
What do you mean?

117
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:01,960
At eight this morning, after breakfast,

118
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:03,400
you accidentally knocked over a vinegar bottle,

119
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:06,520
but it fell perfectly into a box and didn't break.

120
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,200
At nine,

121
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,600
when you took out the trash,

122
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,720
a slipper near the door propped it open,

123
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,720
so you didn't get locked outside.

124
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:19,360
At noon when you were about to do laundry,

125
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,400
you got a phone call,

126
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:24,080
which reminded you to take your phone out of the dirty laundry pocket.

127
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:29,760
Those are just coincidences.

128
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:31,040
Exactly.

129
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:34,400
But no one is naturally unlucky.

130
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,720
What we consider bad luck

131
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:38,160
is just a series of coincidental events stacking up.

132
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:40,960
You're just overly focused on these incidents.

133
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:43,680
This mental block changes your magnetic field

134
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,560
and attracts even more unfortunate events.

135
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:47,880
What are you saying?

136
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:50,040
This sounds like a self-help cliché!

137
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,360
Why do I feel like believing you

138
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,760
is less effective than going to a temple to pray?

139
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:58,160
It's because you can't see the changes in the magnetic field

140
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,600
that you start believing in these illusory things.

141
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:07,200
I can tell you very clearly,

142
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:08,640
judging by the changes in your energy field,

143
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:11,080
something joyful is about to happen to you.

144
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,080
Qi Xiaomiao,

145
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,400
you've won!

146
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,800
You've scored tickets to Allen's concert!

147
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:24,760
Really?

148
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:26,440
Wait a moment,

149
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,280
let me check.

150
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,000
What do you think?

151
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,640
Hao Ruichi,

152
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,520
you're amazing!

153
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:39,960
It's simple.

154
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,160
Am I dreaming?

155
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:44,840
For something like this to happen to you,

156
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:46,480
it sure feels unreal.

157
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,920
I can't believe that over such a small thing,

158
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:53,000
you're all this happy.

159
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,200
You Earthlings,

160
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:55,880
are indeed quite peculiar.

161
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,040
Earthlings?

162
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,280
Oh, and who is this handsome guy?

163
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,760
I am an envoy from the Blue Core Star.

164
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,680
He's just an old classmate of mine from the countryside.

165
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:06,960
Recently, he came to the city and didn’t have a place to stay,

166
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:08,440
so he's sharing a rental with me at my place.

167
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,480
We're roommates now.

168
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:11,840
I,

169
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:18,360
have a feeling there's more to your relationship.

170
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,440
More to it?

171
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,200
It's simpler than your name itself.

172
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,320
I see it’s getting late.

173
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:24,200
We should head home now.

174
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:25,680
See you at the concert!

175
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:26,360
Wait,

176
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:29,560
you hardly get new friends visiting,

177
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:32,040
so I’ve got to let you taste my newly invented dish!

178
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,680
Qi Miao, stop right there!

179
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:36,520
This time my dish is really delicious!

180
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,199
Next time, definitely next time!

181
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:53,280
Not a single customer during meal rush hour?

182
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:56,160
Am I really not cut out for cooking?

183
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:02,080
What's that?

184
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:16,320
Who’s there?

185
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:17,640
Who are you?
